            along dim will sum to 1).

    Returns:
        a Tensor of the same dimension and shape as the input, with
        values in the range [0, 1]

    Examples::

        >>> m = nn.Softmin(dim=1)
        >>> input = torch.randn(2, 3)
        >>> output = m(input)

